From 87ba2193ec83b7950ccfe310c2a1bab9eaeb2357 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zenium Upstream Port <upstream-port@zenium.invalid>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:34:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 85/93] video/mt6768: give videox the include set its ported object needs, so the whole tree builds

drivers/misc/mediatek/video/Makefile descends both mt6768/dispsys/ and mt6768/videox/, and
videox/ has built disp_helper.o since 0081. Its ccflags list, though, was three -I paths.
0084 replaced dispsys/display_recorder.h with the vendor file, and that header includes
"mmprofile.h" - which lives in drivers/misc/mediatek/mmp/, absent from the videox list - so
from 0084 on,

  make ARCH=arm64 drivers/misc/mediatek/video/

failed with `fatal error: mmprofile.h: No such file or directory` while every gate that named
only .../dispsys/ stayed green: disp_helper.c reaches that header through dispsys, and the
dispsys Makefile does advertise mmp/. The next wall behind it was the same story for ion.h
(drivers/staging/android/mtk_ion/, reached via ddp_info.h). The series therefore could not
be built as a whole from 0084 on, even though each of its slices passed its own gate.

Fix: generate videox/Makefile with the same include set l2slice.py computes for dispsys
(stock dispsys + stock videox -I lists, filtered to directories that exist in this tree),
keeping `obj-y += disp_helper.o`. Both directories include each other's headers, so a
per-directory subset was never going to work; the vendor tree gets away with it because its
videox/Makefile gets mmp via MTK_PLATFORM-wide paths the port does not carry.

Exactly one file changes (git diff HEAD~1 HEAD --name-only = that Makefile); no source file
is touched, and no dispsys input or flag moves.

Gate (compile, not link), run in the tree whose tip this commit is: object directories
cleared, then `make -k ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-buildroot-linux-gnu-
drivers/misc/mediatek/video/ drivers/mailbox/ drivers/soc/mediatek/ drivers/misc/mediatek/
smi/ drivers/misc/mediatek/m4u/` -> rc=0, 0 error: lines, 15/15 expected objects present and
non-empty (the 14 dispsys objects plus disp_helper.o at 72,904 B), and 257 link-visible
(T/D/B/R) definitions with 0 duplicates across BOTH directories. The 3 disp_helper_* names
the 0084 census classed as "provider landed, not built here" now have providers in-tree.
Warnings: 107 lines, all attributable and none new as behaviour - 60 from cmdq/v3/
cmdq_record.h and 45 from cmdq_helper_ext.h (the v3 headers carried by 0084, unchanged here),
1 from disp_helper.c:290 -Wimplicit-fallthrough in vendor code as it stands (the
DISP_OPT_PERFORMANCE_DEBUG case has no break; first ever build of this file surfaced it),
1 from ddp_debug.c:594 -Wsizeof-pointer-memaccess (landed in 0084, inputs unchanged by this
patch). CONFIG_WERROR=n so none is fatal; none is silenced or edited away.

Process fix that came out of it, so this class cannot hide again: l2-slice-gate.sh now builds
the PARENT drivers/misc/mediatek/video/ and derives the expected object list from the obj-y
of every landed Makefile in the slice (dispsys + videox) instead of one hand-named directory;
undeps.py accepts several object directories, so a symbol satisfied by a sibling is no longer
counted as a blocker.

NOT functional on hardware. No claim about display output, panel or backlight behaviour, and
a per-directory build implies no vmlinux/Image link.
---
 .../mediatek/video/mt6768/videox/Makefile     | 40 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6768/videox/Makefile b/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6768/videox/Makefile
index 973420b18..9a6f85a5b 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6768/videox/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6768/videox/Makefile
@@ -1,9 +1,39 @@
-# disp_helper.o: the display option table the M4U client reads
-# (DISP_OPT_USE_M4U). Videox itself - mtkfb.o, primary_display.o and the rest
-# of the legacy fb path - is not ported.
-
+#
+# MT6768 videox objects ported so far: the display option table only.
+#
+# disp_helper.o carries DISP_OPT_USE_M4U and friends, which five of the dispsys
+# core objects call (disp_helper_get_option/_stage/_init); the rest of the legacy
+# fb path (mtkfb.o, primary_display.o, ...) is deliberately not ported.
+#
+# Generated by upstream-port/bin/l2slice.py. The include set is the same one the
+# dispsys Makefile carries, because disp_helper.c reaches display_recorder.h in
+# video/mt6768/dispsys/, and that header in turn includes mmprofile.h
+# (drivers/misc/mediatek/mmp/) and, through ddp_info.h, ion.h
+# (drivers/staging/android/mtk_ion/). Both directories therefore need both lists;
+# a per-directory -I set built only from the stock videox Makefile was missing mmp
+# and broke `make drivers/misc/mediatek/video/` from 0084 onwards. Paths are
+# filtered to directories that exist in this tree.
+#
 ccflags-y += -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/include \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/common \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/common/rdma20 \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/common/wdma20 \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/common/layering_rule_base/v1.1 \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6768/videox \
              -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6768/dispsys \
-             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/include
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/base/power/include \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/smi \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/iommu \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/staging/android/mtk_ion \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/cmdq/v3 \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/include \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/m4u/2.0 \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/m4u/mt6768 \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/mmp \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/lcm/inc \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/devfreq \
+             -I$(srctree)/include/linux/soc/mediatek \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/include/mt-plat \
+             -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/cmdq/v3/mt6768
 
 obj-y += disp_helper.o
-- 
